- op: discuss  # 307e
  at: '2026-08-06T03:32:43Z'  # 307e
  by: agent  # 307e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 307e
  clock: 5  # 307e
  nonce: 307e  # 307e
  message: "A/B RUN, express + apollo-server, dev 25ef8937c5. OUTCOME: no_move. Tag stripped. Nothing to\nretract — the PR explicitly declined to claim a recall improvement and tagged this as owed, and\nthe A/B confirms that framing exactly. Full write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/WI-nonad-AB.md\n\nCAPABILITY MOVED, and by a lot:\n  express (all .js)     : 0 -> 154 DDG edges over 25 symbols\n  apollo-server (js+ts) : 1790 DDG edges over 155 symbols\n  dataflow_coverage now reports javascript dataflow_capable=True, blockers=[] on both.\nControl: the synthetic mod.js fixture yields 2 edges / 1 symbol, so the probe fires on a known\npositive before any null is believed.\n\nADJUDICATION DID NOT MOVE: 0 of 4 findings changed. express 3 rows, apollo 1 row, every one\n`structural`, not a single `ddg` or `ddg_mixed`.\n\nCAUSE, read per-flow against source (L55) rather than tallied. All four have a FILE-ANCHOR source\nsymbol, e.g. javascript:examples/cookies/index.js:1-1:file:file. Checked against the code —\nexpress/examples/cookies/index.js:13 reads `process.env.NODE_ENV` at MODULE TOP LEVEL, outside any\nfunction. The D15 file anchor becomes the caller, and `fn_has_ddg = source_fn in analyzed` can\nnever be true for it because build_repo_ddg walks function_node_types and emits only `...:function`\nsymbols. This is a structural limit of an INTRAPROCEDURAL analysis, not a JavaScript wiring gap,\nand it applies to every language.\n\napollo-server's finding is doubly out of scope: smoke-test.mjs is not matched by the spec's `*.js`\nglob at all — the limitation the PR declared rather than assumed, now observed in the wild.\n\nSIZED COHORT-WIDE rather than left at \"4 of 4 on two repos\". Pooled over the four cohort repos\nthat produce findings, 189 evidence rows:\n\n  source symbol kind   rows   adjudicable?\n  function             108    yes\n  method                50    yes\n  external_symbol       18    NO\n  file                  13    NO\n  -> file anchors 13/189 (6.9%); + external_symbol 31/189 (16.4%) un-adjudicable by construction.\n  Per repo: express 3/3 (100%), apollo 1/1 (100%), pretix 9/171 (5%), caddy 0/14 (0%).\n  Method split: structural 79, ddg_mixed 105, ddg 5.\n\nThe JavaScript repos are 100% file-anchor, which is precisely why this A/B reads as no-move: the\nun-adjudicable shape is concentrated in the language the change targeted.\n\nFILED:\n  WI-tizig-fidur-robod-lokal-mohig-zomun-rujan-sudah (P2) — the non-function source-symbol\n    limitation, language-agnostic, 16.4% of pooled rows. Three candidate responses, none chosen;\n    option (b) (walk module scope) can SUPPRESS and must be direction-argued and sized first.\n  WI-fovus-fomil-rigiz-fidin-hulab-midub-hohok-dilon (P3) — the .mjs/.cjs/.jsx glob gap. Note the\n    two interact: apollo's .mjs finding is ALSO module-scope, so fixing the glob alone changes\n    nothing there. They must not be measured as if either alone were sufficient.\n\nINSTRUMENT NOTE, recorded because it nearly produced a false finding. My first probe read\n`getattr(ddg, \"edges\", [])`; the real attributes are ddg_edges / ddg_symbols, so the default\nsilently returned [] and the probe reported ZERO DDG edges for express, apollo-server AND python —\na clean, confident, entirely fabricated zero that would have read as \"the wiring is inert\". Caught\nonly because a Python control was run alongside and Python is known to work. A defaulting getattr\non an attribute name you have not verified is a null-manufacturing device."  # 307e
